{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>At that time HaShem set apart the tribe of Levi.</b> He says: at the time Israel served the calf, the Holy One, blessed be He, set apart the Levites, who had not sinned in it. And so he mentioned above (Deuteronomy 9:20): ״ואתפלל גם בעד אהרן בעת ההיא״. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted that this verse is juxtaposed to the return of the sons of Ya'akan, to teach you that in this matter too the Levites stood firm in their faith and did not stray to turn back as Israel did." "<b>To bear the ark of the covenant of HaShem.</b> These are the Levites. <b>To stand before HaShem to minister to Him.</b> These are the priests. And this is <b>and to bless in His name,</b> for the priests would bless Israel in His name, as it is written (Numbers 6): ״ושמו את שמי״." "<b>Until this day.</b> For Eleazar would raise his hands in his father's stead, as he mentioned above: ״ויכהן אלעזר בנו תחתיו״, and he would fill his place in every matter of the priesthood."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:47:12.769910531Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}